## 3. Usage Guide

### Single prompt (start a new chat)
```bash
node deepseek.js "What is the capital of France?"
```

### Continue an existing session
```bash
node deepseek.js --session e416bae7-... "What is the capital of Germany?"
```

### Edit your last message in that session
```bash
node deepseek.js --session e416bae7-... --edit "Corrected: Capital of Italy?"
```

### List recent sessions to pick one
```bash
node deepseek.js --list
```
Outputs something like:
```
📋 Recent chat sessions:
  [0] Termux CLI Greeting
  [1] Capital of Turkey
  [2] Code merge discussion
```
You can then use `--session` with the ID from the URL of the desired chat (not the index – the index is just for reference). In the future we could add navigation by index, but for now, copy the session ID from the address bar.

### Loop mode (continuous prompts)
```bash
node deepseek.js --session bed16882-... --loop
```
Then type prompt after prompt. Each reply will be printed before the next input prompt appears.  
Use **Ctrl+C** to exit.

