## 4. How It Solves Your Issues

| Problem | Solution |
|--------|----------|
| Reply not captured | `MutationObserver` watches the DOM and sets a global variable. Puppeteer polls until `__deepseekDone` is true. Works reliably even if stop button vanishes instantly. |
| Multiple browser tabs | The `--loop` mode uses a **single browser/page** for an entire session, no extra tabs. |
| Stale sessions / re‑login | The browser profile (`./browser-data`) persists your login indefinitely. No need to re‑export cookies unless you explicitly log out. |
| Session selection | `--list` shows titles and indexes; you can open the matching chat in your mobile browser to copy its ID, or we could later add navigation by index. |
| Edit & resend | `--edit` clicks the pencil, types into the edit textarea, and clicks the update (checkmark) button. The observer captures the new reply. |
| Looping for code merges | `--loop` keeps the same chat open and sends as many prompts as you want, perfect for iterative development. |

