## 3. How to Use the Captured Data

Open `upload-api.json` – you’ll see something like:

```json
{
  "uploadRequest": {
    "url": "https://chat.deepseek.com/api/v0/file/upload_file",
    "method": "POST",
    "headers": {
      "x-ds-pow-response": "eyJhbG...",
      "x-file-size": "23",
      "x-model-type": "default",
      "content-type": "multipart/form-data; boundary=..."
    },
    "postData": "------WebKitFormBoundary...\r\nContent-Disposition: form-data; name=\"file\"; filename=\"upload-test.txt\"\r\nContent-Type: text/plain\r\n\r\nHello from capture script\r\n------WebKitFormBoundary..."
  },
  "uploadResponse": {
    "status": 200,
    "body": "{\"id\":\"file-abc123\",\"name\":\"upload-test.txt\",...}"
  }
